<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Keeps the kinowo dashboard running on http://127.0.0.1:8788 (/nixos and /mobile).

  Same shape as ~/bitcashier/version-dashboard/com.kinowo.version-dashboard.plist, with one
  difference that matters: the PORT. That dashboard already holds 8787 on this workstation, and two
  agents racing for one port means whichever loses exits and launchd retries it for ever, quietly,
  because a bind failure looks exactly like a crash. Different estate, different port.

  Runs `tsx src/server.ts` under Homebrew's node, NOT `tsx watch`. A watch restart kills the process
  under whatever it is doing, which would cut a NixOS switch off mid-ssh. Code changes go live
  through `npm run restart` instead, which sends SIGTERM; the server then refuses new checks and
  switches, lets running ones finish, and exits, and KeepAlive starts the new code. ExitTimeOut is
  above the longest job (a switch, 30 min) so launchd never SIGKILLs a drain in progress.

  PATH IS SET EXPLICITLY because launchd does not read a login shell profile. The server shells out
  to `nix` (the flake roster), `git` (how far behind main; the mobile release tags) and `ssh` (the
  fleet Prometheus, which binds a private address, and the check/switch jobs). Without the Nix
  profile on PATH the roster query fails and every row renders as "not reporting": a page that looks
  like a fleet-wide outage but is really a missing binary.

  NOTE ON THIS COMMENT: XML forbids a double hyphen inside a comment, so none appears here. An
  earlier version used them as dashes and launchctl rejected the whole file as malformed.

  A sibling watchdog (com.kinowo.nixos-dashboard-watchdog) restarts a process that is alive but no
  longer answers /healthz.

  Install:  npm run service install     (copies both plists and loads them)
  Status:   npm run service status
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.kinowo.nixos-dashboard</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/node</string>
    <string>/Users/pawel/projects/movies/infra/version-dashboard/node_modules/.bin/tsx</string>
    <string>src/server.ts</string>
  </array>

  <!-- The flake is resolved as this directory's parent and the repository as its grandparent, so a
       different cwd would make `nix eval` run against whatever tree launchd happened to start in. -->
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/pawel/projects/movies/infra/version-dashboard</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/nix/var/nix/profiles/default/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>

  <key>ExitTimeOut</key>
  <integer>2000</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/pawel/.kinowo-dashboard-logs/server.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/pawel/.kinowo-dashboard-logs/server.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
